  "article_text": "By GMA News Published September 9, 2026 9:19am\nUpdated September 9, 2026 3:09pm\nSome roads in Metro Manila got flooded on Wednesday, September 9, 2026, due to heavy rains from the Southwest Monsoon (Habagat).\nThe Metropolitan Manila Development Authority (MMDA) said it deployed a mobile pump in the E. Rodriguez-Araneta Avenue area in Quezon City to reduce the accumulated water and speed up its discharge toward the nearest waterway\nNag-deploy ang Metropolitan Manila Development authority (MMDA) ng mobile pump sa E-Rodriguez-Araneta Avenue, Quezon City, kasunod ng biglaang pagbuhos ng malakas na ulan sa ilang bahagi ng Metro Manila.\nIsinagawa ang hakbang na ito upang mapababa agad ang naipong tubig at… pic.twitter.com/oce0g7zUTU\n— Official MMDA (@MMDA) September 9, 2026\nBelow is a list of flooded areas, based on information gathered by GMA News and Super Radyo dzBB on the ground and from local government units and government agencies:\nMalabon City\nRizal Ave Extn Brgy San Agustin - Gutter deep Passable to all type of Vehicles as of 2:47 p.m.\nTañong F. Sevilla Blvd. (Bayan) - Gutter deep Passable to all type of Vehicles as of 2:47 p.m.\nMarikina City\nMarcos Highway Underloop - Gutter Deep, Passable to all type of Vehicles as of 2:47 p.m.\nRefresh this page for updates. —KG, GMA News",
